Concrete/README.md:676:**For slice 2, integers complete (all widths u8–u64, i8–i64): provided on LCB's verified path (Apple AArch64).** LCB's verified profile now has `word` (32-bit) and `long` (64-bit) values, `add sub mul and or xor`, the shifts `shiftLeft logicalRight arithmeticRight` (count modulo the width), `mulHighUnsigned mulHighSigned` (accepted only at `long`), division and remainder (`unsignedDiv unsignedRem signedDiv signedRem`; a zero divisor or signed minimum by −1 is stuck, so the adapter must branch to a trap before them), and the comparisons `eq unsignedLT unsignedLE signedLT signedLE` (word result). The adapter will carry every integer as a `long`: exact for types up to 32 bits; 64-bit overflow uses the high multiply and, for add/sub, `xor`/`and`/compare. Still absent and optional while every integer is a `long`: width conversion (`word`↔`long` extension and truncation).
