ConcreteSpec/README.md:1:# Reading the Concrete specification
ConcreteSpec/README.md:2:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:3:**Status: PROPOSED.** This is the specification of the new compiler, written in Lean (decision
ConcreteSpec/README.md:4:rows Q9.15, P3: Lean is the specification). It is not normative until the owner freezes Core at
ConcreteSpec/README.md:5:stage A2c (row Q9.19). Before that, the owner approved the Core design provisionally (A2a,
ConcreteSpec/README.md:6:2026-11-05), and A2b formalized it here and checked the four design theorems (row Q9.14).
ConcreteSpec/README.md:7:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:8:## How to read it
ConcreteSpec/README.md:9:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:10:[`Spec.lean`](Spec.lean) is the specification library (row Q9.15; split into modules by owner
ConcreteSpec/README.md:11:decision 2026-11-06). It imports the modules under [`Spec/`](Spec/) in reading order, and each
ConcreteSpec/README.md:12:module's header says what it covers. Every rule is a Lean definition with a plain-English doc
ConcreteSpec/README.md:13:comment, followed by example programs: the surface program in a doc comment, its Core form, and
ConcreteSpec/README.md:14:what the rules say about it: accepted (`check p = true`) with its outcome (`run p 10 = .exit 42`),
ConcreteSpec/README.md:15:or refused (`check p = false`). You can read it without reading any proof.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:16:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:17:[`Proofs/`](Proofs/) says why the rules hang together. Read it only to check a claim.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:18:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:19:**The owner view.** `scripts/spec/lean_site.sh [OUT]` (after `lake build ConcreteSpec`) generates
ConcreteSpec/README.md:20:a static HTML view into `_build/spec-site/`: every module rendered from its source (doc comments as
ConcreteSpec/README.md:21:prose, rules and examples as code with linked names), each declaration with what it uses and which
ConcreteSpec/README.md:22:proofs are about it, and a page of all theorems with their statements. It is generated from the
ConcreteSpec/README.md:23:sources and the elaborated environment only, and fails on a broken link.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:24:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:25:The decisions are cited by row id (Q1.1 … Q9.19, P1 … P23, in
ConcreteSpec/README.md:26:[docs/decisions.md](../docs/decisions.md)) and by rule id (ODnn, TYPE-n, OWN-n, …, in the
ConcreteSpec/README.md:27:archived prose specification [legacy/docs/spec](../legacy/docs/spec)).
ConcreteSpec/README.md:28:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:29:## Rules of the file
ConcreteSpec/README.md:30:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:31:- Only Lean core is imported, no Mathlib (Q9.16). No `sorry`, no `native_decide` (Q9.17), and
ConcreteSpec/README.md:32:  `autoImplicit` is off, so a misspelled name is an error, never a silently bound variable.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:33:- Axioms: only Lean's standard `propext`, `Quot.sound` and `Classical.choice`. The evaluator
ConcreteSpec/README.md:34:  `run`, the checker `check` and the other executable definitions use `propext` alone, so they
ConcreteSpec/README.md:35:  stay executable and the examples are decided by running them; `Classical.choice` appears only
ConcreteSpec/README.md:36:  in proofs (`rep_roundtrip` through the core lemma `Nat.mod_mul`, and the range proofs).
ConcreteSpec/README.md:37:- These rules are checked in CI by [scripts/proofs](../scripts/proofs): the per-theorem axiom
ConcreteSpec/README.md:38:  inventory against its golden list, the transitive ban on `sorry` and `native_decide`, a fresh
ConcreteSpec/README.md:39:  kernel replay with `leanchecker`, and an independent re-check of the exported theorems by
ConcreteSpec/README.md:40:  con-leche and nanoda.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:41:- The judgments (inductive relations) are the normative form; the checker is proved to agree with
ConcreteSpec/README.md:42:  them (`check_iff`).
ConcreteSpec/README.md:43:- Build: `lake build ConcreteSpec`. The external checker re-checks every theorem.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:44:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:45:## What remains open
ConcreteSpec/README.md:46:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:47:The parts are separate Core fragments, each defined only as far as its theorems need (R4 F8);
ConcreteSpec/README.md:48:unifying them into one Core is A2i work (R-0571).
ConcreteSpec/README.md:49:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:50:Open obligations, by name:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:51:
ConcreteSpec/README.md:52:- **O1 Elaboration** from surface syntax to Core: how literals get a type, how names become
ConcreteSpec/README.md:53:  identities, how nested expressions and grouping become A-normal form, source positions, and that
ConcreteSpec/README.md:54:  acceptance of a source program does not depend on how the elaborator names temporaries.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:55:- **O2 The lexer, model-translation and native-image obligations.**
ConcreteSpec/README.md:56:- **O3 Instrumentation erasure** (Q9.10): the ownership instrumentation (`Slot.moved`, the
ConcreteSpec/README.md:57:  `used`, `live`, `known` and `kfields` fields of `Entry`) is stated as intent, with no erasure
ConcreteSpec/README.md:58:  definition or theorem yet. (Brand erasure, part 5, is done.)
ConcreteSpec/README.md:59:- **O4 Trap diagnostics** (Q7.10, OD101): the bytes of the trap line, including the trap's source
ConcreteSpec/README.md:60:  location (needs O1's positions), and of the startup refusal.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:61:- **O5 Target observations** (the launcher contract): every result here is about the model's
ConcreteSpec/README.md:62:  outcomes; a claim about an executable needs a transport to the approved launcher contract.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:63:- **O6 Launch validation** (part 6): `ProgOk` assumes a valid launch: instance limits, the target
ConcreteSpec/README.md:64:  offering each parameter type, and the launcher's grant minting are not modelled; nor are
ConcreteSpec/README.md:65:  authority rule 11, foreign calls, trait dispatch, generic methods and generated cleanup.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:66:- **O7 Capabilities in the other parts**: the cleanup calls of part 3 and the allocator
ConcreteSpec/README.md:67:  operations of part 5 need capabilities; part 6 checks capabilities in its own fragment only
ConcreteSpec/README.md:68:  (unification, A2i).
ConcreteSpec/README.md:69:- **O8 Part 3** abstracts each deferred call to its identity, dependencies, loans and whether it
ConcreteSpec/README.md:70:  traps; it does not model the statements between registrations or evaluating a `return` value
ConcreteSpec/README.md:71:  before cleanup.
ConcreteSpec/README.md:72:- **O9 Part 4**: the run-time fragment (`vrun`) and the access rules (`Ok`) are separate
ConcreteSpec/README.md:73:  fragments, not yet joined in one soundness theorem (A2i); the run covers array sources (text
ConcreteSpec/README.md:74:  views share the index arithmetic, and their validity is `text_view_utf8`); views of views,
ConcreteSpec/README.md:75:  writes through text views, and text whose length is known while its bytes are not (treated as
ConcreteSpec/README.md:76:  unknown) are not modelled; the frame theorem covers bodies that access only their view. That
ConcreteSpec/README.md:77:  compiled code performs the same range check is a compiler-slice obligation (O5).
ConcreteSpec/README.md:78:- **O10 Part 5** abstracts the condition of `while`: loop test number `k` takes the outcome
ConcreteSpec/README.md:79:  `σ k`, and the results hold for every `σ`.
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:1:#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:2:# FRESH KERNEL RE-CHECK: the built specification replayed through Lean's kernel from nothing, with
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:3:# leanchecker (the lean4checker that ships in the toolchain; no Mathlib).
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:4:#
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:5:# lake build checks each declaration once, as it is elaborated; what lands in the .olean files is
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:6:# whatever the elaborator added. A declaration added without checking (`debug.skipKernelTC`, or a
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:7:# metaprogram calling the kernel's unchecked add) is in the environment unchecked, and it can carry
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:8:# no axiom at all, so scripts/proofs/axioms.sh cannot see it. Replaying the stored declarations
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:9:# through the kernel can.
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:10:#
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:11:#   P  every module the ConcreteSpec sources declare is in the root's import closure, so replaying
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:12:#      the root replays all of them (the closure itself is listed from the environment);
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:13:#   F  `leanchecker --fresh ConcreteSpec`: every constant of the root's closure, Lean core included,
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:14:#      re-added to an EMPTY kernel environment, in dependency order;
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:15:#   M  `leanchecker ConcreteSpec`: every ConcreteSpec module's own declarations replayed on top of its
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:16:#      imports, module by module (the mode that names the module at fault).
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:17:#
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:18:# THE MODULE LIST COMES FROM THE SOURCES (ISS-0016). Given a prefix, leanchecker replays every .olean
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:19:# on its search path under that prefix. The build directory also holds .olean files of modules whose
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:20:# source was deleted or renamed (the CI lake cache restores an older build through a restore-key
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:21:# prefix), so trusting it replays modules that no longer exist: CI run 42424028055 failed on
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:22:# ConcreteSpec.Spec.Ownership after its rename to Slice1Ownership. Both legs therefore run on a staged
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:23:# library holding the .olean files of exactly the modules the sources declare (spec_modules), with the
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:24:# package's build directory replaced by the stage in LEAN_PATH, and M checks that the replayed set is
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:25:# exactly that list. scripts/proofs/lib.sh also prunes orphaned build files before building.
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:26:#
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:27:# NEGATIVE CONTROL: a throwaway package of this toolchain with two modules. ReplayGood proves a true
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:28:# statement honestly; ReplayBad adds `ReplayBad.forged : False` with `debug.skipKernelTC` and proves
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:29:# a theorem from it. Both build, and the forged theorem uses no axiom (so the axiom inventory would
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:30:# pass it). leanchecker must accept ReplayGood and reject ReplayBad at the forged declaration, in
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:31:# both modes. ORPHAN CONTROL: that forged module planted as an orphan under ConcreteSpec/ in a copy of
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:32:# the build directory fails an unfiltered replay of the copy, and the staged replay of the same copy
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:33:# ignores it and passes; a stage missing a source module is refused.
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:34:set -uo pipefail
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:35:source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../checks/lib/gate_env.sh" || exit 2
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:36:ROOT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../.." && pwd)"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:37:cd "$ROOT_DIR"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:38:CHECK_NAME=PROOF-KERNEL-REPLAY
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:39:source scripts/proofs/lib.sh
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:40:
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:41:echo "=== P: population ==="
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:42:population imported > "$TMP/imported.txt" || { no "PROOF_MODE=imported failed"; finish; }
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:43:GAP=$(closure_gap "$TMP/imported.txt")
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:44:[ -z "$GAP" ] && ok "all $(spec_modules | grep -c .) ConcreteSpec source modules are in the closure the replay reads" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:45:  || no "source modules outside the import closure of ConcreteSpec: $(echo $GAP)"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:46:
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:47:echo "=== F/M: replay ==="
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:48:spec_modules > "$TMP/modules.txt"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:49:PKG_LIB="$ROOT_DIR/.lake/build/lib/lean"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:50:TOOL_PATH="$("$LAKE" env printenv LEAN_PATH)" || { no "lake env printenv LEAN_PATH failed"; finish; }
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:51:# stage_lib FROM DEST < MODULES: copy each listed module's .olean files (FROM/A/B.olean*, no .hash)
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:52:# into DEST. A listed module with no .olean is a problem line; nothing unlisted is copied.
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:53:stage_lib() {
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:54:  local from="$1" dest="$2" m p f n
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:55:  mkdir -p "$dest"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:56:  while read -r m; do
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:57:    p="${m//.//}"; n=0
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:58:    for f in "$from/$p".olean "$from/$p".olean.*; do
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:59:      case "$f" in *.hash) continue ;; esac
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:60:      [ -f "$f" ] || continue
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:61:      mkdir -p "$dest/$(dirname "$p")"; cp "$f" "$dest/$(dirname "$p")/" && n=$((n+1))
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:62:    done
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:63:    [ "$n" -gt 0 ] || echo "no .olean for source module $m under $from"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:64:  done
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:65:}
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:66:# staged_path STAGE: LEAN_PATH with the package's build directory replaced by STAGE (exactly once).
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:67:staged_path() {
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:68:  printf '%s' "$TOOL_PATH" | tr ':' '\n' | awk -v pkg="$PKG_LIB" -v st="$1" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:69:    '$0 == pkg { print st; n++; next } { print } END { if (n != 1) exit 1 }' | paste -sd: -
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:70:}
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:71:# replay_problems EXPECTED REPLAYED-OUTPUT: the module sets differ, as one line per difference.
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:72:replay_problems() {
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:73:  sed -n 's/^replaying \(ConcreteSpec[^ ]*\).*/\1/p' "$2" | sort -u > "$2.set"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:74:  comm -23 "$1" "$2.set" | sed 's/^/not replayed: /'
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:75:  comm -13 "$1" "$2.set" | sed 's/^/replayed but not a source module: /'
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:76:}
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:77:leancheck() { # LEAN_PATH args...
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:78:  local lp="$1"; shift; "$LAKE" env env LEAN_PATH="$lp" leanchecker "$@"; }
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:79:STAGE="$TMP/stage"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:80:out="$(stage_lib "$PKG_LIB" "$STAGE" < "$TMP/modules.txt")"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:81:[ -z "$out" ] || { no "staging the source modules: $(echo $out)"; finish; }
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:82:SPATH="$(staged_path "$STAGE")" || { no "LEAN_PATH ($TOOL_PATH) does not name $PKG_LIB exactly once"; finish; }
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:83:ok "staged the $(grep -c . "$TMP/modules.txt") source modules' .olean files; LEAN_PATH reads the stage, not the build directory"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:84:t0=$SECONDS
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:85:leancheck "$SPATH" --fresh ConcreteSpec > "$TMP/f.out" 2>&1; rc=$?
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:86:[ "$rc" = 0 ] && ok "leanchecker --fresh ConcreteSpec: the whole closure re-checked from an empty kernel environment ($((SECONDS-t0))s)" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:87:  || no "leanchecker --fresh ConcreteSpec failed (rc=$rc): $(tail -5 "$TMP/f.out" | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:88:t0=$SECONDS
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:89:leancheck "$SPATH" --verbose ConcreteSpec > "$TMP/m.out" 2>&1; rc=$?
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:90:diff_m="$(replay_problems "$TMP/modules.txt" "$TMP/m.out")"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:91:NREP=$(grep -c . "$TMP/m.out.set")
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:92:[ "$rc" = 0 ] && [ -z "$diff_m" ] \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:93:  && ok "leanchecker ConcreteSpec: exactly the $NREP source modules replayed on their imports ($((SECONDS-t0))s)" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:94:  || no "leanchecker ConcreteSpec: rc=$rc, $NREP modules replayed; $(echo $diff_m) $(grep -v '^replaying' "$TMP/m.out" | tail -5 | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:95:
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:96:echo "=== negative control: a declaration added without kernel checking ==="
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:97:C="$TMP/control"; mkdir -p "$C"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:98:cp lean-toolchain "$C/"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:99:cat > "$C/lakefile.toml" <<'EOF'
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:100:name = "replay-control"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:101:[[lean_lib]]
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:102:name = "ReplayGood"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:103:[[lean_lib]]
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:104:name = "ReplayBad"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:105:EOF
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:106:cat > "$C/ReplayGood.lean" <<'EOF'
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:107:theorem ReplayGood.honest : 2 + 2 = 4 := rfl
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:108:EOF
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:109:cat > "$C/ReplayBad.lean" <<'EOF'
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:110:import Lean
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:111:open Lean Elab Command
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:112:set_option debug.skipKernelTC true in
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:113:run_cmd liftCoreM <| addDecl <| .thmDecl {
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:114:  name := `ReplayBad.forged, levelParams := [], type := mkConst ``False, value := mkConst ``True.intro }
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:115:theorem ReplayBad.anything : 1 = 2 := False.elim ReplayBad.forged
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:116:#print axioms ReplayBad.anything
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:117:EOF
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:118:if (cd "$C" && "$LAKE" build ReplayGood ReplayBad > build.out 2>&1); then
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:119:  has_match -F "'ReplayBad.anything' does not depend on any axioms" < "$C/build.out" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:120:    && ok "control: the forged theorem builds and depends on no axiom (the axiom inventory cannot see it)" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:121:    || no "control: unexpected axiom report for the forged theorem: $(grep -i axiom "$C/build.out" | head -2 | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:122:  for mode in --fresh ""; do
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:123:    (cd "$C" && "$LAKE" env leanchecker $mode ReplayGood) > "$TMP/g.out" 2>&1; rg=$?
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:124:    (cd "$C" && "$LAKE" env leanchecker $mode ReplayBad) > "$TMP/b.out" 2>&1; rb=$?
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:125:    [ "$rg" = 0 ] && ok "control: leanchecker ${mode:-(per module)} accepts the honest module" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:126:      || no "control: leanchecker ${mode:-(per module)} rejected the honest module (rc=$rg): $(tail -3 "$TMP/g.out" | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:127:    [ "$rb" != 0 ] && has_match -F "(kernel) declaration type mismatch, 'ReplayBad.forged'" < "$TMP/b.out" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:128:      && ok "control: leanchecker ${mode:-(per module)} rejects the forged declaration (rc=$rb)" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:129:      || no "control: leanchecker ${mode:-(per module)} on the forged module: rc=$rb: $(tail -3 "$TMP/b.out" | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:130:  done
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:131:  echo "=== orphan control: a build-directory module with no source ==="
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:132:  O="$TMP/orphan-lib"; cp -a "$PKG_LIB" "$O"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:133:  cp "$C/.lake/build/lib/lean/ReplayBad.olean" "$O/ConcreteSpec/Spec/OrphanControl.olean"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:134:  leancheck "$(staged_path "$O")" --verbose ConcreteSpec > "$TMP/o1.out" 2>&1; r1=$?
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:135:  [ "$r1" != 0 ] && has_match -F "(kernel) declaration type mismatch, 'ReplayBad.forged'" < "$TMP/o1.out" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:136:    && ok "control: an unfiltered replay of the build directory replays the planted orphan and fails (rc=$r1)" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:137:    || no "control: the planted orphan did not fail an unfiltered replay (rc=$r1): $(tail -3 "$TMP/o1.out" | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:138:  OS="$TMP/orphan-stage"; out="$(stage_lib "$O" "$OS" < "$TMP/modules.txt")"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:139:  leancheck "$(staged_path "$OS")" --verbose ConcreteSpec > "$TMP/o2.out" 2>&1; r2=$?
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:140:  [ -z "$out" ] && [ "$r2" = 0 ] && [ -z "$(replay_problems "$TMP/modules.txt" "$TMP/o2.out")" ] \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:141:    && [ ! -e "$OS/ConcreteSpec/Spec/OrphanControl.olean" ] \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:142:    && ok "control: the staged replay of the same directory ignores the orphan and replays exactly the source modules" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:143:    || no "control: staged replay with a planted orphan: rc=$r2 $out $(replay_problems "$TMP/modules.txt" "$TMP/o2.out" | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:144:  PB="$TMP/prune-build"; mkdir -p "$PB/lib" "$PB/ir/ConcreteSpec/Spec"; cp -a "$PKG_LIB" "$PB/lib/lean"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:145:  for x in olean ilean trace olean.hash; do echo x > "$PB/lib/lean/ConcreteSpec/Spec/OrphanControl.$x"; done
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:146:  echo x > "$PB/ir/ConcreteSpec/Spec/OrphanControl.c"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:147:  pout="$(prune_orphans "$PB")"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:148:  left="$(find "$PB" -name '*Orphan*' | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:149:  kept="$(stage_lib "$PB/lib/lean" "$TMP/prune-kept" < "$TMP/modules.txt")"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:150:  [ -z "$left" ] && [ -z "$kept" ] && [ "$(grep -c '^pruned orphan' <<< "$pout")" = 5 ] \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:151:    && ok "control: prune_orphans removes the 5 planted orphan files and keeps every source module's .olean" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:152:    || no "control: prune_orphans left '$left', lost '$kept', said: $(echo $pout)"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:153:  PF="$TMP/prune-failclosed"; mkdir -p "$PF/lib"; cp -a "$PKG_LIB" "$PF/lib/lean"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:154:  before="$(find "$PF" -type f | wc -l)"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:155:  for bad in 'echo ConcreteSpec.Spec.Basics' 'printf "ConcreteSpec\nConcreteSpec.Spec.NoSource\n"' 'false'; do
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:156:    ( spec_modules() { eval "$bad"; }; prune_orphans "$PF" ) > /dev/null 2>&1; rp=$?
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:157:    [ "$rp" != 0 ] && [ "$(find "$PF" -type f | wc -l)" = "$before" ] \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:158:      && ok "control: prune_orphans refuses a bad source list ($bad) and deletes nothing" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:159:      || no "control: prune_orphans with a bad source list ($bad): rc=$rp, files $before -> $(find "$PF" -type f | wc -l)"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:160:  done
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:161:  { cat "$TMP/modules.txt"; echo ConcreteSpec.Spec.NoSuchModule; } | sort > "$TMP/modules-plus.txt"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:162:  out="$(stage_lib "$PKG_LIB" "$TMP/missing-stage" < "$TMP/modules-plus.txt")"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:163:  has_match -F "no .olean for source module ConcreteSpec.Spec.NoSuchModule" <<< "$out" \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:164:    && ok "control: a source module with no built .olean is refused, not skipped" || no "control: missing module staged silently: $out"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:165:  printf 'replaying ConcreteSpec.Spec.Basics\n' > "$TMP/short.out"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:166:  [ -n "$(replay_problems "$TMP/modules.txt" "$TMP/short.out")" ] \
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:167:    && ok "control: a replay that skips source modules is refused by the set comparison" || no "control: short replay accepted"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:168:else
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:169:  no "control: the control package did not build: $(tail -5 "$C/build.out" | tr '\n' ' ')"
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:170:fi
scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh:171:finish
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:1:#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:2:# AXIOM INVENTORY: every theorem of the specification depends, transitively, on no axiom beyond
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:3:# propext, Quot.sound and Classical.choice (Q9.17), and the per-theorem inventory equals the golden
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:4:# list scripts/proofs/axioms.golden.
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:5:#
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:6:#   P  population: every module the ConcreteSpec sources declare is in the root's import closure (a
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:7:#      module outside it is neither built by default nor read here), and every module whose file
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:8:#      declares a theorem contributes one, so the population cannot shrink unnoticed;
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:9:#   A  every theorem's transitive axioms (Lean.collectAxioms) are among the standard three;
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:10:#   G  the inventory (`<theorem>\t<axioms>`) equals axioms.golden byte for byte. A theorem added,
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:11:#      removed or renamed, or one that starts or stops using an axiom, changes the golden in the same
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:12:#      commit, where review sees it. `--update` rewrites it from the build.
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:13:#
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:14:# NEGATIVE CONTROLS run the same code on bad inputs and require the failure: an axiom declared and
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:15:# used by a control theorem fails A naming it; new theorems, a private one included, differ from the
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:16:# golden; a golden missing a theorem, carrying an extra one, or
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:17:# recording other axioms fails G; a control module outside the import closure fails P.
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:18:set -uo pipefail
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:19:source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../checks/lib/gate_env.sh" || exit 2
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:20:ROOT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../.." && pwd)"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:21:cd "$ROOT_DIR"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:22:CHECK_NAME=PROOF-AXIOMS
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:23:source scripts/proofs/lib.sh
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:24:GOLDEN=scripts/proofs/axioms.golden
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:25:
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:26:population theorems > "$TMP/inv.tsv" 2> "$TMP/inv.err" \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:27:  || { cat "$TMP/inv.err" >&2; echo "error: the enumerator failed" >&2; exit 2; }
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:28:if [ "${1:-}" = --update ]; then
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:29:  { echo "# Per-theorem transitive axioms of ConcreteSpec (scripts/proofs/axioms.sh). Regenerate with"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:30:    echo "# bash scripts/proofs/axioms.sh --update; review every changed line."
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:31:    cat "$TMP/inv.tsv"; } > "$GOLDEN"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:32:  echo "wrote $GOLDEN ($(grep -c . "$TMP/inv.tsv") theorems)"; exit 0
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:33:fi
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:34:
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:35:# nonstandard FILE → the theorems of an inventory with an axiom outside the standard three
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:36:nonstandard() {
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:37:  awk -F'\t' -v std=" $STANDARD_AXIOMS " '{ n = split($2, a, " ")
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:38:    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) if (index(std, " " a[i] " ") == 0) { print $1 " (" a[i] ")"; break } }' "$1"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:39:}
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:40:# golden_diff INVENTORY GOLDEN → the differing lines, empty when equal
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:41:golden_diff() { diff <(grep -v '^#' "$2") "$1" | grep '^[<>]'; }
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:42:
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:43:echo "=== P: population ==="
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:44:population imported > "$TMP/imported.txt" || { no "PROOF_MODE=imported failed"; finish; }
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:45:GAP=$(closure_gap "$TMP/imported.txt")
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:46:[ -z "$GAP" ] && ok "all $(spec_modules | grep -c .) ConcreteSpec source modules are in the root's import closure" \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:47:  || no "source modules outside the import closure of ConcreteSpec: $(echo $GAP)"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:48:population modules > "$TMP/env-modules.txt" || { no "PROOF_MODE=modules failed"; finish; }
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:49:grep -rlE '^\s*(@\[[^]]*\]\s*)?(private |protected )*theorem ' ConcreteSpec ConcreteSpec.lean --include='*.lean' \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:50:  | sed -E 's#\.lean$##; s#/#.#g' | sort -u > "$TMP/src-modules.txt"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:51:UNSEEN=$(comm -13 <(sort -u "$TMP/env-modules.txt") "$TMP/src-modules.txt")
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:52:NTHM=$(grep -c . "$TMP/inv.tsv")
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:53:[ -s "$TMP/src-modules.txt" ] && [ -z "$UNSEEN" ] && [ "$NTHM" -ge 100 ] \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:54:  && ok "$NTHM theorems from all $(grep -c . "$TMP/src-modules.txt") source modules that declare one" \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:55:  || no "population: $NTHM theorems; modules declaring theorems but absent: $(echo $UNSEEN)"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:56:
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:57:echo "=== A: standard axioms only ==="
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:58:BAD=$(nonstandard "$TMP/inv.tsv")
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:59:[ -z "$BAD" ] && ok "every theorem's transitive axioms are among $STANDARD_AXIOMS ($(cut -f2 "$TMP/inv.tsv" | tr ' ' '\n' | grep . | sort | uniq -c | awk '{printf "%s%s %s", s, $2, $1; s=", "}'))" \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:60:  || no "theorems using a non-standard axiom: $(echo $BAD | cut -c1-400)"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:61:
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:62:echo "=== G: golden list ==="
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:63:[ -f "$GOLDEN" ] || { no "$GOLDEN is missing (bash scripts/proofs/axioms.sh --update)"; finish; }
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:64:D=$(golden_diff "$TMP/inv.tsv" "$GOLDEN")
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:65:[ -z "$D" ] && ok "the inventory equals $GOLDEN ($NTHM theorems)" \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:66:  || no "the inventory differs from $GOLDEN (< golden, > build; regenerate with --update and review): $(printf '%s\n' "$D" | head -10 | tr '\t\n' ' |')"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:67:
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:68:echo "=== negative controls ==="
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:69:cat > "$TMP/c-axiom.lean" <<'EOF'
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:70:axiom ConcreteSpecControl.extra : 1 = 2
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:71:theorem ConcreteSpecControl.usesExtra : 2 = 1 := ConcreteSpecControl.extra.symm
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:72:EOF
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:73:population theorems "$TMP/c-axiom.lean" > "$TMP/c-axiom.tsv" 2>"$TMP/c-axiom.err"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:74:CB=$(nonstandard "$TMP/c-axiom.tsv")
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:75:[ "$CB" = "ConcreteSpecControl.usesExtra (ConcreteSpecControl.extra)" ] \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:76:  && ok "control: a theorem using a declared axiom is refused, and only it ($CB)" \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:77:  || no "control: the extra-axiom theorem was not refused alone: '$CB' $(head -2 "$TMP/c-axiom.err")"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:78:cat > "$TMP/c-clean.lean" <<'EOF'
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:79:theorem ConcreteSpecControl.clean : 1 = 1 := rfl
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:80:private theorem ConcreteSpecControl.hidden : 2 = 2 := rfl
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:81:EOF
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:82:population theorems "$TMP/c-clean.lean" > "$TMP/c-clean.tsv" 2>/dev/null
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:83:# A private name carries the file it was declared in (`_private.<file>.0.…`); the temporary copy's
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:84:# name is random, so it is normalized before the comparison.
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:85:D=$(golden_diff "$TMP/c-clean.tsv" "$GOLDEN" | sed -E 's/^> _private\..*\.0\.ConcreteSpecControl\./> _private.0.ConcreteSpecControl./')
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:86:[ "$D" = "$(printf '> ConcreteSpecControl.clean\t\n> _private.0.ConcreteSpecControl.hidden\t')" ] \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:87:  && ok "control: a new theorem, even axiom-free and even private, is a golden difference" \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:88:  || no "control: new public and private theorems gave the diff '$D'"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:89:FIRST=$(head -1 "$TMP/inv.tsv" | cut -f1)
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:90:grep -vF -- "$FIRST	" "$GOLDEN" > "$TMP/g-missing"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:91:[ -n "$(golden_diff "$TMP/inv.tsv" "$TMP/g-missing")" ] \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:92:  && ok "control: a golden missing a theorem ($FIRST) differs" || no "control: a golden missing $FIRST compared equal"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:93:awk -F'\t' 'BEGIN{OFS="\t"} !/^#/ && !done && $2 == "" { $2 = "propext"; done = 1 } { print }' "$GOLDEN" > "$TMP/g-axiom"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:94:! cmp -s "$GOLDEN" "$TMP/g-axiom" && [ -n "$(golden_diff "$TMP/inv.tsv" "$TMP/g-axiom")" ] \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:95:  && ok "control: a golden recording other axioms for a theorem differs" || no "control: a changed axiom set compared equal"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:96:printf '%s\n' ConcreteSpec ConcreteSpec.Spec > "$TMP/imp-short.txt"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:97:[ -n "$(closure_gap "$TMP/imp-short.txt")" ] \
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:98:  && ok "control: source modules outside a (truncated) import closure are reported" || no "control: a truncated closure reported no gap"
scripts/proofs/axioms.sh:99:finish
