ISSUES.tsv:19:ISS-0015	2026-11-06	ci	Sandboxes inherit the caller's git environment. scripts/checks/review_tool.sh isolated git config only, not the repository-locating variables; a pre-push hook of a LINKED worktree exports GIT_DIR=<repo>/.git/worktrees/<name>, so every git -C <sandbox> in the check acted on the caller. On 2026-11-06 `train.sh ci laudit` run from the linked worktree ~agent/audit-records made the hook's review_tool.sh create its test branches (nonff, capped, parse-*) and set core.bare=true in ~agent/audit-clone (kept unchanged as evidence), and push 28 commits to origin refs/notes/concrete-review (tip b4b364f4, pre-leak 5b6add0d) and 12 to refs/notes/concrete-review-findings (tip 21c56796, pre-leak fd3c6451), authored Review Gate, 17:16:49-17:17:43Z, annotating 21 sandbox commits that exist on no remote (first counted as 22, which wrongly included c54679c3, a real commit whose note at 17:21Z is legitimate); no earlier note was deleted or changed and every reader looks notes up by exact SHA, so none can count as provenance for a real commit. lambdaclass has no notes refs. Codex confirmed with a bounded reproducer on concrete-ci-2 at main f9a8c333 (caller refs and refs/notes/* changed: LEAK) and an independent GIT_DIR experiment. landing_script.sh and landing_bot.sh unset only five of git's local variables; legacy_frozen.sh, acceptance.sh, run-at-ref.sh and bot.sh unset none. Second incident, same cause: the first reproducer installed a pre-push hook that ran review_tool.sh; the leaked GIT_DIR made each nested push re-enter that hook, the recursion exhausted fede-256gb (load ~1900) and the OOM killer took down the orchestrator's session. Structural owner: the sandbox helper scripts/checks/lib/git_sandbox.sh (unsets every `git rev-parse --local-env-vars` variable), sourced by every repository-making script; reproducers and tests run with no installed hook, under timeout 120 and a 512-task / 8G systemd scope bound, or a finite cgroup memory.max plus a p