branches/A-gate-spec-diff.diff:80:+   `compileCore : ConcreteSpec.Program → Except String Concrete.BIR.Program`, in `spec_diff.lean`, is **the** integration point for Core→BIR lowering. It currently returns `no Core→BIR lowering yet (slice 1)`. The gate checks generation, acceptance, oracle exits and construct coverage, and loudly reports `spec leg: 0 programs compiled`; it never claims a spec/native comparison passed. The branch that adds lowering (slice-1 work, no owner yet) must fill this hook and make compiled programs required. The driver then emits the same native artifacts, with status, empty stdout and stderr derived from the SPEC outcome (a trap uses the runtime line for the lowered site), so no new comparison path is needed.
branches/A-gate-spec-diff.diff:84:+   `SPEC_DIFF_SECS` (default 600) bounds the shared build, generation, controls and comparisons; `SPEC_DIFF_N` (default 300) caps candidates per leg, and too few judged programs is INCOMPLETE, never a pass. Outcome and construct counts are printed. A mismatch prints the seed, index, Lean term, exact `bir:` manifest row and `Concrete.BIR.Examples` entry to save as a regression. Controls require LLVM overflow removal and LCB exit-off-by-one to fail for those planted reasons (the latter in both native and evaluator legs), require a planted spec exit+1 expectation to be rejected against the spec-derived outcome, and check same-seed byte determinism and different-seed variation. Mutation flags are unavailable on normal driver commands and require the explicit planted-control command.
